# The projection manifest fixtures are DIGEST-BEARING CONTENT, not text.
#
# Generation 2 names generation 1 by a sha256 over generation 1's exact bytes, and generation 3 names
# generation 2 the same way. That chain is the thing the succession rules are built on, so a checkout that
# rewrote LF to CRLF would change the bytes, change the digest, and break the chain — on Windows only, with a
# failure that reads like a contract defect rather than like a line-ending conversion.
#
# This is deliberately the NARROWEST possible rule. It covers one fixture directory whose files are content
# addressed by their own bytes. It is not a repository-wide line-ending policy: every other file in this
# repository is still handled exactly as it was, and the CRLF-tolerance the rest of the suites were written
# for is unchanged. `test/projection-manifest-v1.ts` asserts these files really did arrive without CR, so a
# future change that defeats this rule fails by name instead of by digest.
test/fixtures/projection-manifest-v1/** -text
